Meeting with San Diego Business Leaders 
					 April 26, 2013  
					Last week, I was pleased to speak at the San Diego Chamber of Commerce’s Annual Congressional Luncheon and Panel.  Along with my San Diego Congressional colleagues, I answered questions about the most pressing issues before Congress and discussed issues vital to Southern California job creation, including:

Moving toward a balanced federal budget;
Immigration reform;
Keeping an eye on how the Administration is  implementing sequestration;
San Ysidro Port of Entry, the Keystone Pipeline and the need to explore domestic projects that will further our economic health;
Entitlement reform as a top priority for getting our fiscal house in order; and,
 The need for policies coming out of Washington to create jobs, reduce federal red tape and encourage small business growth.

